  <!-- About: Playback Speed Calculator -->
  <section id="about-playback-speed" class="section-container" style="padding: var(--spacing-3xl) var(--spacing-lg); background-color: var(--color-canvas); max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm); font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-link);">About</div>
    <h2 style="font-size: var(--font-size-heading-xl); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-xl); line-height: var(--line-height-heading-xl); color: var(--color-ink); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);">Playback Speed Calculator — Watch Less, Learn More</h2>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-body-lg); line-height: var(--line-height-body-lg); color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);">
      Real Playback Speed is a free online calculator that tells you how long any video or audio will take at a different playback speed, and how much time you’ll save. Enter the original duration, pick a speed, and see the adjusted time instantly — no “Calculate” button required.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-heading-md); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-md); color: var(--color-ink); margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-sm);">What Is Playback Speed?</h3>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md); color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);">
      Playback speed is the rate at which media plays relative to its original recording. At 1.0x, content plays at normal speed. At 1.5x, a 60-minute video finishes in 40 minutes. At 2.0x, it finishes in 30 minutes. Our calculator lets you enter the original duration and your chosen speed, then shows the adjusted duration, time saved, and percentage saved as you type.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-heading-md); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-md); color: var(--color-ink); margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-sm);">YouTube URL Duration Detection</h3>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md); color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);">
      Paste a public YouTube video URL (watch, youtu.be, or shorts) and the calculator attempts to detect the video’s duration automatically, filling in Hours, Minutes, and Seconds. This works for most public videos. It does not work for private, age-restricted, or members-only content, and YouTube occasionally blocks automated detection. If detection fails, you can enter the duration manually.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-heading-md); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-md); color: var(--color-ink); margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-sm);">How to Use the Calculator</h3>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md); color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);">
      1. Enter the original media length in Hours, Minutes, and Seconds.<br />
      2. Choose a playback speed from 0.25x to 4.0x using the slider or preset buttons.<br />
      3. Read the new duration, time saved, and percentage saved in real time.<br />
      4. Switch to Target Time mode to find the exact speed required to finish within your available window.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md); color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);">
      The calculator runs entirely in your browser with no account required. It supports three modes: standard duration calculation, reverse target-time mode, and playlist batch mode.
    </p>
  </section>

