  <!-- FAQ: Playback Speed Calculator -->
  <section id="playback-speed-faq" class="section-container" style="padding: var(--spacing-3xl) var(--spacing-lg); background-color: var(--color-canvas-elevated); max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm); font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-link);">FAQ</div>
    <h2 style="font-size: var(--font-size-heading-xl); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-xl); line-height: var(--line-height-heading-xl); color: var(--color-ink); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-lg); text-align: center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        What is playback speed?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Playback speed is the rate at which media plays relative to its original recording. At 1.0x, content plays at normal speed. At 1.5x, a 60-minute video finishes in 40 minutes; at 2.0x, it finishes in 30 minutes.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        How fast is 1.5 playback speed?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        At 1.5x, content plays 50% faster than normal. A 60-minute video takes 40 minutes, a 30-minute video takes 20 minutes, and a 90-minute video takes 60 minutes.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        How do I calculate time saved at a different speed?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Divide the original duration by the playback speed. For example, 60 minutes ÷ 1.5 = 40 minutes. Time saved is the original duration minus the adjusted duration — in this case, 20 minutes saved.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        Which playback speed is normal?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Normal playback speed is 1.0x — the original recording speed with no acceleration or slowdown.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        How do I find the speed needed to finish within a time limit?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Divide the original duration by your target time. A 90-minute video you want to finish in 45 minutes needs 90 ÷ 45 = 2.0x. Use the Target Time mode to calculate this automatically.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        Does playback speed affect watch time?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Yes. Watching at a faster speed reduces total watch time because the same content plays in less time. A 60-minute video at 1.5x results in 40 minutes of watch time.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        How long is 1 hour in 1.5 speed?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        One hour at 1.5x playback speed takes 40 minutes. You save 20 minutes. 60 minutes ÷ 1.5 = 40 minutes.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        Can I calculate multiple videos at once?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        Yes. Playlist Batch mode lets you enter several video durations and see the total adjusted time and time saved across all of them at your chosen speed.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); overflow: hidden;">
      <summary style="padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-ink); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; outline: none;">
        How to increase playback speed shortcut?
      </summary>
      <div style="padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg); font-size: var(--font-size-body-md); color: var(--color-body); line-height: var(--line-height-body-md);">
        On YouTube in a web browser, hold Shift and press the greater-than key to increase speed, or Shift and the comma key to decrease it. Our site supports keyboard shortcuts: press 1–8 for preset speeds, C to copy, R to reset, and Tab to switch calculator modes.
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

